BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (curriculum alignment consulting, billed per project.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our early pricing assumption is a license in the range of several hundred dollars per) Tj T* (instructor per year, with conversion packages priced by the number of recipes. These numbers) Tj T* (come from conversations with a small number of instructors and are not yet tested with real) Tj T* (purchase decisions. We expect programs to buy through department budgets or career and) Tj T* (technical education funds, which can mean slow sales cycles.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Instructors currently use general recipe costing tools designed for restaurants, spreadsheets) Tj T* (they build themselves, or the costing exercises that come with textbooks. Restaurant costing) Tj T* (software is powerful but is built for operators, not for teaching, and it does not generate) Tj T* (lesson plans or student assignments. Spreadsheets are flexible and free but time-consuming, and) Tj T* (they do not handle allergens or pricing updates well. Textbook exercises are easy to adopt but) Tj T* (use fixed prices that quickly become stale.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our advantage is that we are built specifically for teaching: recipes become assignments,) Tj T* (students see live cost data, and allergens are part of the same workflow. A weakness is that) Tj T* (larger software companies could add an education mode to existing products, and we have not yet) Tj T* (shown that instructors will pay for something they can partly do with spreadsheets. Our pricing) Tj T* (data also depends on third-party sources, which we are still evaluating for cost and) Tj T* (reliability.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Danielle Okafor-Reyes is a culinary arts graduate student at our university and a former line) Tj T* (cook and kitchen supervisor. She leads curriculum design and instructor relationships. Marcus) Tj T* (Tillbrook is a computer science senior who built the prototype and leads product development.) Tj T* (Priya Venkataraman studies business and handles customer interviews, pricing, and financial) Tj T* (planning. We have not yet added an advisor from the foodservice industry, though we are) Tj T* (speaking with two possible candidates. None of us has run a company before.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have defined the core concept and built a working prototype that handles recipe entry,) Tj T* (ingredient costing with unit conversion, food-cost percentage, and allergen flagging. We have a) Tj T* (basic website describing the service. Instructors at two programs, one community college and) Tj T* (one private school, have used the prototype with a total of roughly forty students in trial) Tj T* (assignments. Feedback so far has been positive about time savings, and instructors asked for) Tj T* (better handling of regional ingredient pricing and support for batch recipes. We have not yet) Tj T* (collected payment from any customer, and we have not formed a legal entity.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our costs so far are small and have been covered personally by the team: hosting, a few) Tj T* (software subscriptions, and travel to visit one program. Over the next twelve months we project) Tj T* (spending mostly on pricing data access, part-time development help, and basic legal and) Tj T* (accounting setup. Our rough target is five paying programs by the end of the first year, which) Tj T* (would bring in revenue in the tens of thousands of dollars, not enough to cover full salaries) Tj T* (but enough to show demand. These projections are early estimates and will change as we learn) Tj T* (more.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking prize funding to cover legal formation of the company, a one-year pricing data) Tj T* (subscription, and paid pilots at three to five additional programs. We would also value) Tj T* (mentorship from people with experience selling software to schools or colleges, introductions) Tj T* (to culinary program directors, and advice on how to structure pricing and contracts for public) Tj T* (institutions. Finally, we would welcome feedback on whether our market is large enough to) Tj T* (support a standalone company or whether we should position Menuschool as a feature within a) Tj T* (broader hospitality education offering.) Tj ET
